James discussed the development of an abstraction around model and tool selection within his AI system, presenting a structured contract for tools that includes detailed specifications on expected tool capabilities and compatibility considerations. He shared the specifics of a web search tool provided by OpenAI, detailing the expected inputs, options, and functionalities available for implementation. I assisted James by drafting a complete tool implementation for the `web_search` tool, exhibiting a well-defined structure to manage settings, validate domains, and extract citations and sources from the response. The developed code aims to ensure effective tool invocation and output handling, reflecting a comprehensive design aligned with James's goals in AI system development.
